    "abstract": "SimCLR learns visual representations by maximizing agreement between two augmented views of the same image with a contrastive loss in a latent space. Key findings: composition of augmentations (especially random crop plus colour distortion) is critical, a learnable nonlinear projection head improves representation quality, and contrastive learning benefits from larger batches and longer training. A linear classifier on SimCLR ResNet-50 features reaches 76.5% top-1 on ImageNet with 4x width.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Composition of data augmentations, notably random cropping plus colour distortion, is crucial for contrastive representation learning.",
      "A learnable nonlinear projection head between representation and contrastive loss substantially improves the representation.",
      "Contrastive learning benefits from larger batch sizes and more training steps than supervised learning.",
      "Linear evaluation of ResNet-50 (4x) SimCLR features reaches 76.5% ImageNet top-1, matching supervised ResNet-50."
    ],
